WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
- Well you got a new single,
with Florida Georgia Line,

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.520
so how did this come about?

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.523
'Cause you have a
friendship with them, right?

00:00:04.523 --> 00:00:06.740
- Yeah of course, um, well um,

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:10.430
me and the boys, we
met actually doing the,

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:13.860
when I was asked to do
the remix of their first

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.440
single that I knew of, "Cruise".

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.050
And fortunately enough,
I did it, and you know,

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.810
we kinda made history coming
together with "Cruise" and,

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:22.730
and we bonded, right
off the gate with that,

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:25.230
with the video, we did
like two tours together,

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.040
and they're family now, man,

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.960
and you know, we've been
together ever since,

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.580
as far as communicating
and keeping in contact.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:33.370
So when I started working on this project,

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:34.780
we came up with this idea, man,

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:36.600
and it was, it was
pretty special, you know.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.430
We hammered it out, and I
wanted it to be my first single

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.460
off of my EP, "Heartland",
coming out top of next year.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:44.726
- [Kelly] That's so awesome.

00:00:44.726 --> 00:00:45.559
- Thank you.

00:00:45.559 --> 00:00:47.760
- And honestly, I mean, even
I've gotten into country,

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.080
but I remember the first
person that I remember

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:52.810
crossing over into country,
doing something like that,

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:53.930
was you, and Tim McGraw,

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:55.090
Like way back in the day.
- Yeah.

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:55.923
- Like that's what,

00:00:55.923 --> 00:00:57.870
so it's so funny that a lot
of people are doing it now,

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.577
but you were kinda the
pioneer of that, I feel like,

00:01:00.577 --> 00:01:01.420
way back in the day.
- Yeah, you know,

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.010
the thing about it is like,

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.510
so, my uncle was the one
that got me into music,

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:07.560
and he was a huge Lionel Richie fan.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:08.393
- [Kelly] Ooh.

00:01:08.393 --> 00:01:10.140
- And Lionel used to do a lot of writing,

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.950
and he wrote for Kenny Rogers,

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:14.000
and he wrote for a lot
of different people.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.130
And, my uncle would play
anything by Lionel Richie.

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:20.360
If it was sung, written,
produced, whatever,

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:21.193
he would play it.

00:01:21.193 --> 00:01:23.500
And he used to play Kenny Rogers a lot,

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:26.360
and I, that was kinda
like how my love affair

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.020
for country music kinda started.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.900
And it's one of the purest art forms

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.310
that still exists to this day.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:33.253
But, I mean, you know--

00:01:33.253 --> 00:01:34.086
- I feel like it's cousins with R&amp;B.

00:01:34.086 --> 00:01:35.873
Like growing up,
- [Nelly] Oh totally, totally.

00:01:35.873 --> 00:01:37.690
I would listen to Trisha
Yearwood and like, Reba,

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:39.240
but also Toni Braxton,
- [Nelly] You nailed it.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.160
- And like Monica and Brandy.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:41.010
I feel like--
- [Nelly] You nailed it.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.070
- It's the storytelling.

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:43.310
- And even if you listen to it,

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:47.090
a lot of the songs that are
traditional, huge R&amp;B hits,

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:50.410
have also been transformed
into country music.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.127
- Remember, like "I Swear",
cross over into both.

00:01:52.127 --> 00:01:53.540
- [Nelly] "I Swear", yep.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:54.710
- Yeah, there was um,

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:57.911
- He did uh, "Lady",
"Lady", Lionel Richie,

00:01:57.911 --> 00:01:59.000
and Commodores did it.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.420
But then him and Kenny Rogers did it.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:05.120
So "I Will Always Love You",
Whitney Houston did it,

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:05.953
- Yeah.

00:02:05.953 --> 00:02:07.140
- Kinda crossed it back over from Dolly's.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.160
- That's 'cause it's all storytelling--

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.250
- From Dolly Parton, so yeah,

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.890
just the love, the passion,
and the honesty in the music

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:14.080
I think, it resonates with me.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:15.130
- Me too, me as well.

